   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 439 of the laws of 2008 relating to authorizing the town of Riga to establish the Host Benefit Agreement reserve fund, in relation to improvements for highways in such town and in relation to making such provisions permanent",
    "basePrintNo": "S1694",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1694-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1, Chap 439 of 2008",
    "lawSection": "Highways",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S1694\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 439 of the laws of 2008\nrelating to authorizing the town of Riga to establish the Host Benefit\nAgreement reserve fund, in relation to improvements for highways in\nsuch town and in relation to making such provisions permanent\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo continue to provide the Town of Riga with the authority to\nappropriate and allocate landfill revenue received from the Host.\nBenefit Agreement with Monroe County through a Host Benefit Agreement\nreserve fund, to expand the types of projects for which the fund can\nbe used, and to repeal the current expiration date.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSECTION 1: amends section 1 of Chapter 414 to make technical\ncorrection to the authority provided under such chapter to add as a\npermitted expenditure payment for the repair and improvement of\nhighways, including sluices, culverts and bridges having a span of\nfive feet or less, in any area of the town.\n\nSECTION 2: provides that such correction shall take effect immediately\nand shall be deemed in full force and effect as of the effective date\nof the initial chapter.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation provides a purely technical correction to clarify\nauthority previously provided to the town of Riga pursuant to Chapter\n414 of the Laws of 2014.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is an amendment of Chapter 414 of the Laws of 2014.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall be deemed to have\nbeen in full force and effect on the same date as Chapter 414 of the\nLaws of 2014 took effect.\n\n",
